3752	                // deterministic is exactly the work owed, not a reason to stop
3753	                // reporting it.
3754	                //
3755	                // AND THE DEFECT IS REAL AND LARGER THAN THIS LINE. Measured
3756	                // 2026-08-24 on the CI-staged SaBRe artifact: a guest that forks
3757	                // and reaps its child with `wait4(WNOHANG)` diverges 36 of 50
3758	                // under `--verify-strict`, while ptrace is 0 of 50 on the same
3759	                // guest. The divergence is not confined to logging -- the guest
3760	                // ITSELF executes different work, 355 syscalls with 4 `wait4`
3761	                // calls in one run against 354 with 3 in the other. The
3762	                // scheduler's committed non-poll decisions are byte-identical
3763	                // (68 in both), so what varies is how many times the parent is
3764	                // told "not yet". Silencing this line would have left that
3765	                // unreported.
